   "text": {
    "L1": "The poem The Swing is full of joy, movement, and a swinging beat.",
    "L2": "The child goes up and down, then back and forth, while the wind rushes past.",
    "L3": "Sway means to move gently from side to side.",
    "L4": "The words sway and day rhyme, and sky and fly rhyme.",
    "L5": "Higher than the birds is playful exaggeration, not an exact measurement.",
    "L6": "It shows that swinging feels very high, fast, and free, like flying.",
    "L7": "For two things, add -er and use than: The swing goes higher than the slide.",
    "L8": "Use one comparison word, not more higher or higher from."
   },
